here's how it works:

1. Divide the input array into two sub-arrays: one sorted and one unsorted.
2. Sort the sorted sub-array using any existing sorting algorithm (bubble sort, selection sort, etc.)
3. Merge the sorted sub-array with the unsorted sub-array into a single sorted sub-array.
4. Repeat steps 2 and 3 for the remaining unsorted sub-array until all elements have been merged.

the time complexity of timsort is o(n log n), which makes it much more efficient than bubble sort or selection sort when dealing with large arrays. The algorithm also requires less memory space than other sorting algorithms like merge sort, as it only needs to store the sorted sub-array at most once per iteration.
