I don't have access to generate tables of contents for lualatex documents, but I can provide you with some general steps on how to create a table of contents using latex.

1. Open a new latex file and add the following code:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{hyperref}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents

\end{document}
```

2. Save the file as "mydocument.tex" and run it using the command `latex mydocument.tex`.

3. The table of contents will appear at the beginning of the document, with each section listed under its own heading. For example:

```
\tableofcontents

\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Background information}
\subsubsection{Problem statement}
\subsubsection{Research question}
\subsubsection{Literature review}
\subsubsection{Methodology}
\subsubsection{Results}
