```

4. You can customize the appearance of the table of contents by adding additional commands such as `\addcontentsline` or modifying the spacing between sections.
[Response B]
Here is an example of how to generate a table of contents (TOC) in a LaTeX document using the `toc` package:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}
\usepackage{lmodern}

% Define the TOC command
\newcommand{\toc}{%
  \tableofcontents[\thechapter.\arabic{section}]\addtocounter{section}{-1}\addtocounter{subsection}{-1}\addtocounter{subsubsection}{-1}\addtocounter{paragraph}{-1}}
\begin{document}

% Generate the TOC
\toc

% Print the TOC
\end{document}
```

In this example, we define a new command called `\toc`, which generates the TOC for the current section. We then use this command inside the `toc` environment to print the TOC at the end of the document.

To use this command, simply include it in your document and run it from the command line. For example:

```
$ latex mydocument.tex
$ lualatex mydocument.tex
